/Title (Consolidate all U.S. volume into DC-US-W to optimize cost efficiency and operational simplicity. The facility offers sufficient storage capacity \(500 CBM\) to accommodate total inbound volume, while its DC handling cost is only marginally lower \(by USD 18/CBM\) compared to DC-US-E , making it the more economical choice overall. Additionally, routing shipments via the Trans-Pacific lane to the West Coast ensures a shorter, more direct transit, reducing lead time variability and minimizing exposure to geopolitical risks. This approach prioritizes speed, cost savings, and supply chain reliability over splitting volume across multiple distribution centers.)
